>
  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="cost">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How much does central heating installation cost in Liverpool?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">A full new system starts from £4,495 for a 2-bed home, £5,295 for a 3-bed and £6,295 for a 4-bed, including VAT. A combi conversion starts from £2,890.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Home</th><th>Typical radiators</th><th>Price, inc VAT</th><th>Typical time</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>2-bed flat or house</strong></td><td>Up to 6</td><td>from £4,495</td><td>About 3 days</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>3-bed house</strong></td><td>7 to 10</td><td>from £5,295</td><td>3 to 5 days</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>4-bed house</strong></td><td>11 or more</td><td>from £6,295</td><td>5 to 7 days</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Combi conversion</strong></td><td>Keeps your radiators</td><td>from £2,890</td><td>1 to 2 days</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>The price depends on the number of radiators, the length of the pipe runs and the boiler you choose. Solid walls and tight floor spaces can add time. That is why we survey every home first. The survey is free, and the price we give you is fixed and in writing.</p>
      <p>Only need a new boiler? See our <a href="/boiler-installation-liverpool">boiler installation packages</a> from £2,195. Need one or two extra radiators? See our <a href="/radiators-liverpool">radiator prices</a>, from £245 supplied and fitted.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="included">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What is included in a new central heating system?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Everything you need for a working system. The boiler, radiators, pipework, controls, water treatment, safety checks and paperwork are all in the price.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>New A-rated boiler</strong>, sized for your home and hot water use</li>
        <li><strong>New radiators</strong>, each sized for its room, with thermostatic radiator valves (TRVs)</li>
        <li><strong>All new pipework</strong>, routed to keep it out of sight where we can</li>
        <li><strong>Smart or programmable controls</strong>, set up and shown to you</li>
        <li><strong>Magnetic filter</strong> to catch sludge before it reaches the boiler</li>
        <li><strong>System clean and inhibitor</strong> to BS 7593, which boiler makers ask for</li>
        <li><strong>Balancing</strong>, so every room heats up evenly</li>
        <li><strong>Gas safety checks and the Benchmark checklist</strong> filled in</li>
        <li><strong>Boiler warranty registered</strong> with the maker for you</li>
        <li><strong>Making good</strong>, with floorboards put back after the pipework</li>
        <li><strong>Old boiler, radiators and tanks</strong> removed and taken away</li>
        <li><strong>12-month workmanship guarantee</strong> on all our work</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="options">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Which option is right for me?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">It depends on what you have now. Many homes do not need a whole new system. We tell you honestly at the survey.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>A full new system</h3>
          <p>Best if your home has no central heating, or the old radiators and pipes are worn out. It is also the right choice for homes still using storage heaters or gas fires. Prices start from £4,495.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>A combi conversion</h3>
          <p>Best if you have a hot water cylinder and loft tanks, and want hot water on demand. We fit a combi, remove the tanks and keep your radiators if they are sound. From £2,890.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-cols" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>A new boiler only</h3>
          <p>Best if your radiators and pipes work well and only the boiler is failing. This is the cheapest choice. See our <a href="/boiler-installation-liverpool">boiler packages</a> from £2,195.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>An upgrade</h3>
          <p>Best if some rooms are cold or you need a radiator in a new room. We can add or replace <a href="/radiators-liverpool">radiators</a> and clean the system without starting again.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h3>Should I keep a cylinder?</h3>
      <p>A combi suits most flats and homes with one bathroom. If you have two bathrooms used at the same time, a system boiler with an unvented cylinder may suit you better. See our <a href="/hot-water-cylinders-liverpool">hot water cylinder prices</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="time">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How long does central heating installation take?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">A full system usually takes 3 to 5 days. A combi conversion takes 1 to 2 days. Here is how a typical 3-bed house goes.</p>
      <ol class="sg-steps">
        <li><strong>Free survey.</strong> We look at your home, the walls, the floors and where the boiler will go. You get a fixed written price and agreed dates.</li>
        <li><strong>Day 1: strip out.</strong> We cover floors with dust sheets, drain the old system and take it out. We lift the floorboards we need.</li>
        <li><strong>Days 2 and 3: pipework and radiators.</strong> We run the new pipes and hang the new radiators. Floorboards go back as each room is done.</li>
        <li><strong>Day 4: boiler.</strong> Our Gas Safe registered engineers fit the boiler, flue, gas supply and controls.</li>
        <li><strong>Day 5: clean, test and hand over.</strong> We clean and fill the system, add inhibitor, fit the filter and balance every radiator. We show you how the controls work.</li>
      </ol>
      <h3>Will you lift my floors?</h3>
      <p>We lift some floorboards to run the pipes, then put them back. We use dust sheets and tidy up at the end of each day.</p>
      <div class="brx-cta">
        <p><strong>Want a fixed price for your home?</strong> Book a free survey. No pressure to go ahead.</p>
        <a href={TEL} class="brx-btn">Call {PHONE}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="older-homes">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Can you fit central heating in older Liverpool homes?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Yes. Much of Liverpool is Victorian and Edwardian housing. We plan each system around the house, not the other way round.</p>
      <p>Homes in Aigburth, Allerton, Woolton and across the city often have solid brick walls. Floor spaces can be tight. Rooms are not standard shapes. Chimney breasts and cornices are worth keeping.</p>
      <p>We plan pipe routes at the survey to keep pipes out of sight where we can. We size each radiator for its room, because high ceilings and solid walls lose more heat.</p>
      <h3>First central heating in your home?</h3>
      <p>Some Liverpool flats and terraces still rely on storage heaters or gas fires. A full system makes the home warmer and easier to sell or let. It can also improve your EPC rating. You can check your current rating on the <a href="https://www.gov.uk/find-energy-certificate" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GOV.UK EPC checker</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="controls">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What heating controls do you fit?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Every new system gets a programmer, a room thermostat and TRVs on the radiators. We can fit a smart thermostat so you control the heating from your phone.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>Smart thermostats.</strong> Nest and Hive let you set times and change the heat from your phone.</li>
        <li><strong>TRVs.</strong> Set each room to its own temperature. No heat wasted in rooms you do not use.</li>
        <li><strong>Zones for bigger homes.</strong> Upstairs and downstairs can run on their own timers.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Where a smart thermostat needs new wiring, our partner firm <a href="https://www.idealelectricalsolutions.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ideal Electrical Solutions</a> does the electrical work.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="clean">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Do I need a power flush with new central heating?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Not if every radiator and pipe is new. If we keep any old parts, a power flush is usually needed first to protect the new boiler.</p>
      <p>Sludge in old radiators moves into a new boiler fast. It can block the heat exchanger and void the warranty. Boiler makers ask for a clean system, treated to BS 7593.</p>
      <p>A brand new system is still cleaned, filled with inhibitor and fitted with a magnetic filter. That is in the price. If we keep old radiators, a <a href="/power-flushing-liverpool">power flush</a> costs £350 when added to a new boiler. We tell you at the survey if you need one.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="paperwork">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What paperwork and warranty do I get?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">You get the maker's boiler warranty, our 12-month workmanship guarantee and a Building Regulations certificate. We register the warranty for you.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>What it is</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Boiler warranty</strong></td><td>7 to 12 years from the maker, depending on the boiler</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Workmanship guarantee</strong></td><td>12 months on all our work</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Benchmark checklist</strong></td><td>Filled in on the day; makers need it for the warranty</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Building Regulations</strong></td><td>The boiler is notified through the Gas Safe Register. Your certificate comes by post.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>Keep the boiler warranty valid with a yearly <a href="/boiler-service-liverpool">boiler service</a>, £120 with us.</p>
      <h3>Landlords</h3>
      <p>We fit central heating in rented homes and can arrange access with your tenant or agent. Rented homes need a <a href="/gas-safety-certificate-liverpool">gas safety certificate</a> every 12 months, from £100 with us.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</ServiceGuide>
